(4863463, 703367, 96614, '<td valign="top">so, 61st eh? i thought i''d do better... oh well =)  ok, so the cat is out of the bag now... you all know how I did it... <br/> <br/>as far as all the comments... some helpful, some not so much...  I am a newbie... and the rules are vague as to whether I can gain depth of field by combining different exposures... yes, I am allowed to do it (now I know...) but honestly, I like it better like this... I LIKE the "Harsh Light" and I LIKE the blur on the box... If you don''t, well, boo hoo to you!  =)   as far as the shot of the city scape... yea, it''s not the best shot, BUT the bristol board was MASSIVE! it was four sheets together, so a total of about 5 feet by 7 feet... I had to assemble them on site because it wouldn''t fir in my car all put together... I needed Two other people to hold it up for me, and that was the only time I could get the help...<br/> <br/>no, as far as the title, some people didn''t like the part I added... yes. I know, i shouldn''t have added it.  It was the second contest I entered and I was still learning about the rules, so I didn''t know what to do, I actually took that "single shot, No editing" out and re-added it like 10 times because I couldn''t make up my mind... it''s not your fault for calling me on it because you didn''t know that i was on''y a week old at the time... If I could  do it again, I would leave that part out for sure...  OH, and to be safe, I submitted teh original fromt he beginning...<br/> <br/>on a side note... If I DID want to put that box in focus (aside from combining multiple pictures with the different scenes in focus...) I would have to have either:<br/>a) had a lens with a f/500 stop<br/>b) stood WAY-WAY-WAY back and used a 5000mm lens to gain the depth of field...<br/> <br/>I just though i''d add that for those of you who seemed to think that it would be possible with one shot  =)      <br/> <br/>I like it much better this way... it draws your attention to the cityscape...<br/> <br/>Thanks everyone for the feedback... I don''t know if anyone will ever read this, but i wanted to add it anyways,  =)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-08-04 07:46:52.</i></td>', 'so, 61st eh? i thought i''d do better... oh well =)  ok, so the cat is out of the bag now... you all know how I did it...  as far as all the comments... some helpful, some not so much...  I am a newbie... and the rules are vague as to whether I can gain depth of field by combining different exposures... yes, I am allowed to do it (now I know...) but honestly, I like it better like this... I LIKE the "Harsh Light" and I LIKE the blur on the box... If you don''t, well, boo hoo to you!  =)   as far as the shot of the city scape... yea, it''s not the best shot, BUT the bristol board was MASSIVE! it was four sheets together, so a total of about 5 feet by 7 feet... I had to assemble them on site because it wouldn''t fir in my car all put together... I needed Two other people to hold it up for me, and that was the only time I could get the help... no, as far as the title, some people didn''t like the part I added... yes. I know, i shouldn''t have added it.  It was the second contest I entered and I was still learning about the rules, so I didn''t know what to do, I actually took that "single shot, No editing" out and re-added it like 10 times because I couldn''t make up my mind... it''s not your fault for calling me on it because you didn''t know that i was on''y a week old at the time... If I could  do it again, I would leave that part out for sure...  OH, and to be safe, I submitted teh original fromt he beginning... on a side note... If I DID want to put that box in focus (aside from combining multiple pictures with the different scenes in focus...) I would have to have either:a) had a lens with a f/500 stopb) stood WAY-WAY-WAY back and used a 5000mm lens to gain the depth of field... I just though i''d add that for those of you who seemed to think that it would be possible with one shot  =)       I like it much better this way... it draws your attention to the cityscape... Thanks everyone for the feedback... I don''t know if anyone will ever read this, but i wanted to add it anyways,  =)', '2008-08-04 08:42:52.000000', '2008-08-04 08:46:52.000000', 0),
(4863469, 703363, 61651, '<td valign="top">I had the exact same idea for this challenge, but when push came to shove, no time to get the shot taken and entered.  Glad to see a camera obscura/pinhole-y shot make it into in this challenge - the perfect, and perfectly appropriate, use of a cardboard box, for DPC!  Really digging that slight Shroud of Turin effect you have going on the far wall of the box.</td>', 'I had the exact same idea for this challenge, but when push came to shove, no time to get the shot taken and entered.  Glad to see a camera obscura/pinhole-y shot make it into in this challenge - the perfect, and perfectly appropriate, use of a cardboard box, for DPC!  Really digging that slight Shroud of Turin effect you have going on the far wall of the box.', '2008-08-04 08:47:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4863472, 703069, 43463, '<td valign="top">One of my top rated images in the challenge. Loved how this composition illustrated many facets of life stages or chapters as you put it in the title. When I first saw this in the challenge it made me think of the Brady Bunch opening formation credits. But instead of just a head portrait you give us far more ''personality'' of the people within the boxes because of the activity they are doing, the expressions, and dress of each person. Tones, lighting, composition of all elements come together in perfect unison. I too was a little confused as to why the two men adorned the opposite and outsides of the box. My conclusion is that you placed them there in that position to act as a Yin &amp; Yang type symbol (one is dressed in dark colors the other in light).</td>', 'One of my top rated images in the challenge. Loved how this composition illustrated many facets of life stages or chapters as you put it in the title. When I first saw this in the challenge it made me think of the Brady Bunch opening formation credits. But instead of just a head portrait you give us far more ''personality'' of the people within the boxes because of the activity they are doing, the expressions, and dress of each person. Tones, lighting, composition of all elements come together in perfect unison. I too was a little confused as to why the two men adorned the opposite and outsides of the box. My conclusion is that you placed them there in that position to act as a Yin & Yang type symbol (one is dressed in dark colors the other in light).', '2008-08-04 08:49:50.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(4863476, 703439, 61651, '<td valign="top">I was one of your 10''s, and the only 10 I gave out for this challenge.  Utterly fantastic, love the surreality and concept, and the processing (Urban Acid, is it?).  Model''s seeming detachment is perfect to get across the sense of surreal.  Will go so far as to say this image is one of my favorites, out of all my favorites.  :)</td>', 'I was one of your 10''s, and the only 10 I gave out for this challenge.  Utterly fantastic, love the surreality and concept, and the processing (Urban Acid, is it?).  Model''s seeming detachment is perfect to get across the sense of surreal.  Will go so far as to say this image is one of my favorites, out of all my favorites.  :)', '2008-08-04 08:54:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(4863478, 703715, 23484, '<td valign="top">Nice job Don and congrats on a great score.</td>', 'Nice job Don and congrats on a great score.', '2008-08-04 08:55:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(4863480, 703709, 23484, '<td valign="top">Nice job Michelle.  The DOF is fantastic. Great score.</td>', 'Nice job Michelle.  The DOF is fantastic. Great score.', '2008-08-04 08:56:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(4863483, 703675, 23484, '<td valign="top">Very interesting perspective Mary.</td>', 'Very interesting perspective Mary.', '2008-08-04 08:57:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4863486, 702600, 23484, '<td valign="top">Very nice unique idea.</td>', 'Very nice unique idea.', '2008-08-04 08:58:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4863487, 703652, 20577, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the top 10. I''m sorry that I had the police come talk to you about this. I didn''t realize that you really don''t make your kids live in boxes. It was an honest mistake. Still friends?</td>', 'Congrats on the top 10. I''m sorry that I had the police come talk to you about this. I didn''t realize that you really don''t make your kids live in boxes. It was an honest mistake. Still friends?', '2008-08-04 08:58:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4863508, 702935, 50695, '<td valign="top">For some reason, I only gave this a 6 and then kept on going, maybe because I wanted to see what that box in the back was. But now I see this as a fascinating attempt to provide a visual metaphor for conceptualization/abstraction.</td>', 'For some reason, I only gave this a 6 and then kept on going, maybe because I wanted to see what that box in the back was. But now I see this as a fascinating attempt to provide a visual metaphor for conceptualization/abstraction.', '2008-08-04 09:07:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(4863538, 703650, 43463, '<td valign="top">Wow! I am impressed with the amount of work and effort you put into this. Congradulations on creating such a wonderful photo. The level of detail in the wings (holy hannah you had a lot of patience with ''carving'' those cardboard feathers), the pose, the expression of the models face -ALL- together is what makes this a fantastic composition. The lighting in this one is also very good for as Icarus ''falls'' the darkness is decending upon him - at least that is the way I read the image. I am glad that your composition did not get slammed by the DNMC crowd. It would be nice if it had placed a little highter BUT you made it into the top 25% and earned over a 6 on the final score. Not to mention the most important thing: you created an image you should be very proud of.</td>', 'Wow! I am impressed with the amount of work and effort you put into this. Congradulations on creating such a wonderful photo. The level of detail in the wings (holy hannah you had a lot of patience with ''carving'' those cardboard feathers), the pose, the expression of the models face -ALL- together is what makes this a fantastic composition. The lighting in this one is also very good for as Icarus ''falls'' the darkness is decending upon him - at least that is the way I read the image. I am glad that your composition did not get slammed by the DNMC crowd. It would be nice if it had placed a little highter BUT you made it into the top 25% and earned over a 6 on the final score. Not to mention the most important thing: you created an image you should be very proud of.', '2008-08-04 09:24:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4863545, 703684, 30861, '<td valign="top">This is terrific. I''m surprised it did not do better actually. Congrats on a finely crafted image :-)</td>', 'This is terrific. I''m surprised it did not do better actually. Congrats on a finely crafted image :-)', '2008-08-04 09:31:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4863549, 703717, 91716, '<td valign="top">This was my fave photo in this challenge, Congratulations!</td>', 'This was my fave photo in this challenge, Congratulations!', '2008-08-04 09:33:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4863554, 703684, 66384, '<td valign="top">You''re right, Shez, I did recognize your beautiful image as being one of your designs. I always love them, and this is no exception.</td>', 'You''re right, Shez, I did recognize your beautiful image as being one of your designs. I always love them, and this is no exception.', '2008-08-04 09:38:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4863576, 703658, 66384, '<td valign="top">Lovely lighting, texture, and rich color. Certainly hard to achieve with cardboard. Also very nice composition. I would have expected this to be 6 or higher.</td>', 'Lovely lighting, texture, and rich color. Certainly hard to achieve with cardboard. Also very nice composition. I would have expected this to be 6 or higher.', '2008-08-04 09:43:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4863584, 703652, 89723, '<td valign="top">Post Challenge comments:<br/> <br/>Thanks for all the comments! I''m really happy to be in the top ten. My photography is like my golf game. 30 or 40 horrible shots with one great one that keeps me coming back!</td>', 'Post Challenge comments: Thanks for all the comments! I''m really happy to be in the top ten. My photography is like my golf game. 30 or 40 horrible shots with one great one that keeps me coming back!', '2008-08-04 09:45:59.000000', NULL, 0),
