(4874883, 703676, 47852, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club!</b> <br/> <br/><u>First Impression:</u> Cute kitty with a natural pose (which can be hard), nice warm colors, nice contrast without blowing out any of the highlights.  Lacks that little extra something to take it to the next level.<br/> <br/><u>Looking Closer:</u>  It looks like you tried to use the rule of thirds with your placement of the cat, but somehow the feel that you usually get with that just isn''t there.  Something feels off... perhaps the corner of the box right in front, also in sharp focus, that divides the shot?  Maybe if you had taken this from a higher angle, or used a shallower dof?  Perhaps playing with a tighter crop could have been an option.  Also, I''m noticing the crinkles and nicks in the box.. not sure if that''s good or bad, just something that caught my attention.<br/> <br/><u>Overall:</u> Not a bad score, but I think it lacked that little extra something to really catch the voters attention.  Looks like many voters gave it a 6, saying it was nicely done and better than average.  Comments seem to indicate the same.<br/> <br/>Hope this has been helpful.  Please feel free to PM me with any questions about this critique.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  First Impression: Cute kitty with a natural pose (which can be hard), nice warm colors, nice contrast without blowing out any of the highlights.  Lacks that little extra something to take it to the next level. Looking Closer:  It looks like you tried to use the rule of thirds with your placement of the cat, but somehow the feel that you usually get with that just isn''t there.  Something feels off... perhaps the corner of the box right in front, also in sharp focus, that divides the shot?  Maybe if you had taken this from a higher angle, or used a shallower dof?  Perhaps playing with a tighter crop could have been an option.  Also, I''m noticing the crinkles and nicks in the box.. not sure if that''s good or bad, just something that caught my attention. Overall: Not a bad score, but I think it lacked that little extra something to really catch the voters attention.  Looks like many voters gave it a 6, saying it was nicely done and better than average.  Comments seem to indicate the same. Hope this has been helpful.  Please feel free to PM me with any questions about this critique.', '2008-08-08 09:34:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4875822, 703709, 30982, '<td valign="top">I didn''t get a chance to vote the challenge but was drawn to this one when I glanced through.  My sister, bless her heart, bought me a box of 64 - I think this was a couple of years after I graduated from college.  :-)  This is not only well done, it brings back very fond memories.  Great light, great choice of DOF.</td>', 'I didn''t get a chance to vote the challenge but was drawn to this one when I glanced through.  My sister, bless her heart, bought me a box of 64 - I think this was a couple of years after I graduated from college.  :-)  This is not only well done, it brings back very fond memories.  Great light, great choice of DOF.', '2008-08-08 16:38:18.000000', NULL, 0),
